{{!-- A1's featured strip: the posts the publication flagged, in a track that scrolls.

	{{> "home/featured"}}

Its own query, and the only one on this Surface that is not the shared post window: "featured"
is a flag on the post, not a position, so `filter="featured:true"` is the whole of it. A post can
be both featured and recent, so a card here may also appear below — which is what the design
draws too.

NO SWIPER. The design source drives this strip with Swiper 11, and the whole of what it uses is
`slidesPerView` with `spaceBetween` plus two buttons calling `slidePrev`/`slideNext`. Native
scroll-snap is the same control with no library: keyboard- and touch-accessible for free, no
width cached at init to re-measure once the webfonts settle, and `prefers-reduced-motion`
honoured by switching the scroll behaviour rather than a speed.

The card widths are Swiper's own arithmetic, written out as the `featured-card` utility in
assets/css/screen.css — three media queries rather than three Tailwind breakpoint variants, for
a reason worth reading there before touching it.

`{{#if featured}}` and not the get's `{{else}}`: get calls `options.inverse` only for an invalid
resource or an API error (core/frontend/helpers/get.js), never for an empty result. Without the
guard, a publication that has flagged nothing renders the heading, its rule, four rem of padding
and two arrow buttons scrolling an empty track. "Featured" is an editorial choice; a publication
that has not made one has no strip. --}}
{{#get "posts" filter="featured:true" limit="6" include="authors,tags" as |featured|}}
	{{#if featured}}
		<section
			aria-labelledby="a1-featured"
			class="container pt-16">
			<div class="border-border flex items-baseline justify-between gap-5 border-b pb-3.5">
				<h2
					id="a1-featured"
					class="font-display text-h2 tracking-heading font-medium">{{t "Featured"}}</h2>

				<div
					data-featured-controls
					class="flex gap-2">
					<button
						type="button"
						data-featured-prev
						aria-label="{{t "Previous featured posts"}}"
						class="btn border-border bg-surface text-text hover:bg-surface-2 rounded-pill grid size-9 cursor-pointer place-items-center border font-mono">
						<span aria-hidden="true">←</span>
					</button>
					<button
						type="button"
						data-featured-next
						aria-label="{{t "Next featured posts"}}"
						class="btn border-border bg-surface text-text hover:bg-surface-2 rounded-pill grid size-9 cursor-pointer place-items-center border font-mono">
						<span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
					</button>
				</div>
			</div>

			{{!-- The padding lives on a wrapper rather than on the track, so the scroll container's
			own box starts exactly where the first card does — padding inside a snap container shifts
			every snap position by that amount. --}}
			<div class="pt-7">
				{{!-- `data-scroll-intent` is read by the responsive audit, not by the browser: a
				scroll container with a hidden scrollbar normally reads as absent content, and this
				one has two arrow buttons above it saying otherwise. Declaring it keeps the audit's
				rule armed everywhere else. --}}
				<div
					data-featured
					data-scroll-intent="carousel with prev/next controls"
					class="snap-track flex gap-5 overflow-x-auto">
					{{#foreach featured}}
						<article class="featured-card">
							<a
								href="{{url}}"
								class="text-text block no-underline">
								{{#if feature_image}}
									<img
										src="{{img_url feature_image size="l"}}"
										{{#if feature_image_alt}}alt="{{feature_image_alt}}"{{else}}alt=""{{/if}}
										loading="lazy"
										decoding="async"
										class="border-border block aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-md border object-cover">
								{{/if}}

								{{#primary_tag}}
									<p class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-accent mt-3.5 uppercase">{{name}}</p>
								{{/primary_tag}}

								<h3 class="font-display tracking-heading mt-2 text-[21px] leading-[1.25] font-medium">{{title}}</h3>

								<p class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted mt-2.5 uppercase">{{> "dateline"}}</p>
							</a>
						</article>
					{{/foreach}}
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	{{/if}}
{{/get}}
